  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144297/assets/4fd99d8e6a64427167fee57e0e0ba7c55cbe9a0bac31157f9692e3cd4a346f00.png)\n\nIf the model above represents $3$ wholes, use the model to solve the following division problem. Express your answer as a whole number.\n\n$3÷\\frac{3}{6}=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "We proceed as follows:\n\n- First, we split each whole into sixths.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144297/assets/d90639c936363a89657dd29172d5fd244b88ddbc80e5c5c2ad3a1b435736ac60.png)\n\n \n\n- Next, we create groups of $\\frac{3}{6}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144297/assets/722e68a49beefa326bddf7f29c374a9b0c274e56a9621092a0dca6b6465e468b.png)\n\n \n\n- Then, we count the groups.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144297/assets/8a13c7877fcbaaac076b55091d39a2a6c92eef5edf2105dcaafb18a9b5415cbc.png)\n\n \n\nSo, if we divide $3$ wholes into groups of $\\frac{3}{6},$ we get $6$ groups in total.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n3÷\\frac{3}{6}=6.\n$$",
